; The domain core. No js_of_ocaml dependency, anywhere below this point --
; `dune build -p symbaroum` is the CI step that keeps it that way.
;
; `unqualified` rather than `qualified`: the subdirectories are there so a reader
; can see the layering, not to add a prefix to every reference. Module names stay
; flat (`Symbaroum.Dice`, not `Symbaroum.Scalars.Dice`), which is how the modules
; already refer to one another and how the plan's target structure names them.
;
; The layering runs strictly downward and is a review rule, not a compiler rule:
;
;   scalars/     -> depend on nothing but Core and each other
;   aggregates/  -> scalars
;   data/        -> scalars, aggregates
;   transitions/ -> everything above
;   codec/       -> everything above; the only place that parses or prints JSON
;
; The one boundary that *is* enforced is the package boundary: this whole
; library must build with `-p symbaroum`, which has no UI library in scope.

(include_subdirs unqualified)

(library
 (name symbaroum)
 (public_name symbaroum)
 (libraries core base_quickcheck splittable_random yojson)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_jane ppx_yojson_conv)))
